{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"When a job in the Gerrit Verified Gate is cancelled or times out, the gate casts `Verified -1`\nwith a message that is exactly `CANCELLED: <run URL>`. It names no job, gives no reason, and\ndoes not say whether the run failed a test, was superseded, or hit a job timeout. An operator\nor agent triaging the change has to open the run and inspect job conclusions by hand to learn\nanything at all.\n\nThis is OBSERVABILITY ONLY. When the gate votes +1 or -1 must not change; only what the -1\nmessage carries.\n\n## Why the message is empty today\n\n`.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`'s `vote` job casts the label with\n`lfreleng-actions/gerrit-review-action`. That action builds its message itself:\n\n    MESSAGE=\"${STATUS}: ${SERVER_URL}/${REPOSITORY}/actions/runs/${RUN_ID}\"\n\nIt exposes no input for custom text. Verified both at the pinned SHA\n(a1c036a59b94c8ab89de26d378f6a28cc7378b13, v1.1.2) and on the action's current main; v1.1.2 is\nthe latest tag, so there is no upstream version to bump to. Its inputs are host, port,\nusername, key, key_name, known_hosts, gerrit-change-number, gerrit-patchset-number, vote-type,\ncomment-only.\n\nNote that the action's `comment-only: true` input does NOT help: it only suppresses the labels\nand still posts the SAME self-built `<STATUS>: <url>` text. It is a label switch, not a message\nswitch. So the enriched comment cannot be delivered through that action at all.\n\n## Evidence this bites\n\nConfirmed cancel/timeout -1s that carried no signal:\n\n- The `bounded mutation gate` job hit `timeout-minutes: 30` (check-run annotation \"The job has\n  exceeded the maximum execution time of 30m0s\"). Gerrit showed only `CANCELLED: <url>`.\n- The `select mutation shards` step failed with\n  `mutation_gate.py: error: argument command: invalid choice: 'select'` on patchsets predating\n  the selector. Again no signal in the vote.\n\nTwo different causes, one indistinguishable message. Only the second needs author action (a\nrebase), and the vote cannot tell them apart.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Add `scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py`, a trusted script with a pure `summarize()` function\n   mapping a GitHub list-jobs payload plus check-run annotations to a short triage summary:\n   one line per non-successful job giving the job name, whether it TIMED OUT (annotation\n   \"exceeded the maximum execution time\") versus was cancelled or failed, its duration, and\n   its `html_url`.\n2. In `vote`, when the normalized vote-type is not `success`, run that script over this run's\n   jobs and post the result to Gerrit with a DEDICATED SSH STEP — the same\n   `ssh ... gerrit review <change>,<patchset> --message '<text>'` call the action makes\n   internally, reusing the existing `vars.GERRIT_SERVER` / `vars.GERRIT_SSH_USER` /\n   `vars.GERRIT_KNOWN_HOSTS` / `secrets.GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY`, passing NO `--label` so it is a\n   comment and not a vote. A REST path is not available: per ADR-0023 the CI account is\n   SSH-key-only with no HTTP password.\n\nThe script is checked out from the default branch via the existing trusted sparse-checkout,\nthe same trust model as `scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py` — patchset-controlled code never\nruns in the vote job.\n\nBecause the summary is interpolated into a single-quoted argument of that remote command, and\nmatrix job names derive from `.github/mutation-shards.toml` (which a patchset controls),\n`summarize()` strips `'`, `\\` and every control character except newline.\n\n## Files\n\n- `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` (vote job: add summary + SSH comment steps and a key\n  cleanup step; extend the sparse-checkout list; add `checks: read` for the annotations read)\n- `scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py` (new)\n- `tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py` (new)\n- `tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_port_heldout.py` (its sparse-checkout assertion\n  becomes structural now that the step fetches two scripts)\n\nDeliberately does NOT touch `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml` or\n`tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` — Gerrit change 1627 owns those.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `summarize()` given a jobs payload containing a job whose annotation says it\n      exceeded its maximum execution time renders that job as timed out, naming the job and\n      its duration; a unit test asserts the rendered text.\n- [ ] AC2: `summarize()` distinguishes the three non-success outcomes — timed out, cancelled\n      without a timeout annotation, and failed — with different wording; unit tests cover all\n      three.\n- [ ] AC3: `summarize()` given a payload where every job succeeded returns an empty string, so\n      a `Verified +1` run posts no extra comment; asserted by a unit test.\n- [ ] AC4: the vote job posts the summary via a dedicated SSH `gerrit review --message` step\n      that passes no `--label` (so it casts neither Verified nor Code-Review) and is guarded on\n      the normalized vote-type not being `success`. Asserted by a test parsing\n      `gerrit-verify.yaml` for that step and failing if `--label`, `Verified=` or\n      `Code-Review=` appears in it.\n- [ ] AC5: the vote-type fed to the existing cast step is byte-identical to today's — the\n      `normalize` step and its inputs are unchanged. Asserted by a test that the cast step's\n      `vote-type` expression still reads `steps.normalize.outputs.vote-type`.\n- [ ] AC6: `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` still passes, i.e. `vote.needs` is unchanged.\n- [ ] AC7: the new steps cannot change the gate outcome — both are `continue-on-error` and run\n      AFTER the cast step, asserted by tests, so a fault in the comment path leaves the vote\n      already cast.\n- [ ] AC8: a job name containing a single quote cannot escape the quoting of the remote\n      command; asserted by a unit test feeding a hostile shard name through `summarize()`.\n\n## Verification\n\n    python -m pytest tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py -q\n    python -m pytest tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py -q\n    python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py\n    python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py\n    make lint && make typecheck"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786521555760241001,"uuid":"41064632-0dd4-4cb5-9974-303578a31486"}